  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "9-math-3-ex4.4-q1",
      "questionNumber": 1,
      "question": "Fill in the blanks to complete the following identities: **(i)** $s^2 - 11s + 24 = (\\_\\_\\_\\_)(\\_\\_\\_\\_)$ **(ii)** $(\\_\\_\\_\\_)(x + 1) = (3x^2 - 4x - 7)$ **(iii)** $10x^2 - 11x - 6 = (2x - \\_\\_\\_)(\\_\\_\\_ + 2)$ **(iv)** $6x^2 + 7x + 2 = (\\_\\_\\_\\_)(\\_\\_\\_\\_)$",
      "solution": [
        {
          "step": 1,
          "content": "**(i) $s^2 - 11s + 24$:** We need two numbers whose sum is 11 and product is 24. These are 3 and 8. Since the middle term is negative, both are negative: $-3$ and $-8$. $$s^2 - 11s + 24 = s^2 - 8s - 3s + 24 = s(s - 8) - 3(s - 8) = (s - 3)(s - 8)$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 2,
          "content": "**(ii) $(\\_\\_\\_\\_)(x + 1) = 3x^2 - 4x - 7$:** Factor the RHS: $$3x^2 - 4x - 7 = 3x^2 - 7x + 3x - 7 = x(3x - 7) + 1(3x - 7) = (3x - 7)(x + 1)$$ So the blank is $(3x - 7)$."
        },
        {
          "step": 3,
          "content": "**(iii) $10x^2 - 11x - 6 = (2x - \\_\\_\\_)(\\_\\_\\_ + 2)$:** Factor: $$10x^2 - 11x - 6 = 10x^2 - 15x + 4x - 6 = 5x(2x - 3) + 2(2x - 3) = (5x + 2)(2x - 3)$$ So $10x^2 - 11x - 6 = (2x - 3)(5x + 2)$."
        },
        {
          "step": 4,
          "content": "**(iv) $6x^2 + 7x + 2$:** $$6x^2 + 7x + 2 = 6x^2 + 3x + 4x + 2 = 3x(2x + 1) + 2(2x + 1) = (3x + 2)(2x + 1)$$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "(i) (s − 3)(s − 8)  (ii) (3x − 7)(x + 1)  (iii) (2x − 3)(5x + 2)  (iv) (3x + 2)(2x + 1)",
      "verified": true,
      "formulaBox": {
        "title": "Splitting the Middle Term",
        "content": "$$x^2 + (a+b)x + ab = (x + a)(x + b)$$"
      },
      "notes": "**Exam Tip:** For $x^2 + px + q$, find two numbers whose sum is p and product is q, then split the middle term."
    },
    {
      "id": "9-math-3-ex4.4-q2",
      "questionNumber": 2,
      "question": "Select and use the identity that will help you to find the following products without multiplying directly: **(i)** $(41)^2$ **(ii)** $(27)^2$ **(iii)** $(23 \\times 17)$ **(iv)** $(135)^2$ **(v)** $(97)^2$ **(vi)** $(18 \\times 29)$ **(vii)** $(34 \\times 43)$ **(viii)** $(205)^2$",
      "solution": [
        {
          "step": 1,
          "content": "**(i) $(41)^2$:** $41 = 40 + 1$. $$(40 + 1)^2 = 40^2 + 2 \\times 40 \\times 1 + 1^2 = 1600 + 80 + 1 = 1681$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 2,
          "content": "**(ii) $(27)^2$:** $27 = 30 - 3$. $$(30 - 3)^2 = 30^2 - 2 \\times 30 \\times 3 + 3^2 = 900 - 180 + 9 = 729$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 3,
          "content": "**(iii) $23 \\times 17$:** Write as $(20 + 3)(20 - 3)$. Using $(a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2$: $$20^2 - 3^2 = 400 - 9 = 391$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 4,
          "content": "**(iv) $(135)^2$:** $135 = 100 + 35$. $$(100 + 35)^2 = 100^2 + 2 \\times 100 \\times 35 + 35^2 = 10000 + 7000 + 1225 = 18225$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 5,
          "content": "**(v) $(97)^2$:** $97 = 100 - 3$. $$(100 - 3)^2 = 100^2 - 2 \\times 100 \\times 3 + 3^2 = 10000 - 600 + 9 = 9409$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 6,
          "content": "**(vi) $18 \\times 29$:** Write as $(20 - 2)(20 + 9)$. Using $(x + a)(x + b) = x^2 + (a + b)x + ab$: $$20^2 + (-2 + 9)(20) + (-2)(9) = 400 + 140 - 18 = 522$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 7,
          "content": "**(vii) $34 \\times 43$:** Write as $(38 - 4)(38 + 5)$. Using $(x + a)(x + b)$: $$38^2 + (-4 + 5)(38) + (-4)(5) = 1444 + 38 - 20 = 1462$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 8,
          "content": "**(viii) $(205)^2$:** $205 = 200 + 5$. $$(200 + 5)^2 = 200^2 + 2 \\times 200 \\times 5 + 5^2 = 40000 + 2000 + 25 = 42025$$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "(i) 1681  (ii) 729  (iii) 391  (iv) 18225  (v) 9409  (vi) 522  (vii) 1462  (viii) 42025",
      "verified": true,
      "notes": "**Exam Tip:** For products of two numbers near a common value, use (x + a)(x + b) = x² + (a + b)x + ab. For squares, split into a round number plus/minus a small number."
    },
    {
      "id": "9-math-3-ex4.4-q3",
      "questionNumber": 3,
      "question": "Factor the following: **(i)** $9a^2 + b^2 + 4c^2 - 6ab + 12ac - 4bc$ **(ii)** $16s^2 + 25t^2 - 40st$ **(iii)** $r^2 - r - 42$ **(iv)** $49g^2 + 14gh + h^2$ **(v)** $64u^2 + 121v^2 + 4w^2 - 176uv - 32uw + 44vw$",
      "solution": [
        {
          "step": 1,
          "content": "**(i) $9a^2 + b^2 + 4c^2 - 6ab + 12ac - 4bc$:** Write $9a^2 = (3a)^2$, $b^2 = b^2$, $4c^2 = (2c)^2$. Cross terms: $2(3a)(-b) = -6ab$, $2(-b)(2c) = -4bc$, $2(3a)(2c) = 12ac$. So: $$= (3a - b + 2c)^2$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 2,
          "content": "**(ii) $16s^2 + 25t^2 - 40st$:** Rearrange as $16s^2 - 40st + 25t^2$. $16s^2 = (4s)^2$, $25t^2 = (5t)^2$, $-40st = -2(4s)(5t)$. So: $$= (4s - 5t)^2$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 3,
          "content": "**(iii) $r^2 - r - 42$:** We need two numbers whose product is $-42$ and sum is $-1$. These are $-7$ and $6$. $$r^2 - r - 42 = r^2 - 7r + 6r - 42 = r(r - 7) + 6(r - 7) = (r - 7)(r + 6)$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 4,
          "content": "**(iv) $49g^2 + 14gh + h^2$:** $49g^2 = (7g)^2$, $h^2 = h^2$, $14gh = 2(7g)(h)$. So: $$= (7g + h)^2$$"
        },
        {
          "step": 5,
          "content": "**(v) $64u^2 + 121v^2 + 4w^2 - 176uv - 32uw + 44vw$:** Rearrange as $64u^2 + 121v^2 + 4w^2 - 176uv + 44vw - 32uw$. Write $64u^2 = (8u)^2$, $121v^2 = (11v)^2$, $4w^2 = (2w)^2$. Cross terms: $2(8u)(-11v) = -176uv$, $2(-11v)(-2w) = 44vw$, $2(8u)(-2w) = -32uw$. So: $$= (8u - 11v - 2w)^2$$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "(i) (3a − b + 2c)²  (ii) (4s − 5t)²  (iii) (r − 7)(r + 6)  (iv) (7g + h)²  (v) (8u − 11v − 2w)²",
      "verified": true,
      "notes": "**Exam Tip:** For three-variable squares, rearrange terms so that the negative cross terms are grouped together before matching the identity."
    }
  ]
}
